    "background_story": "Kyree was a brilliant and eccentric paleontologist who spent his life studying the ancient creatures of the Mesozoic era. His obsession with the archidiskidon, a prehistoric armored fish, led him to spend years excavating fossils in the depths of the Amazon rainforest. Kyree's colleagues often joked that he was as armored as his beloved archidiskidon, with a tough exterior that hid a sharp mind and a passion for discovery. His tireless efforts finally paid off when he uncovered a nearly complete archidiskidon fossil, which he named 'Amazonia'. The discovery sent shockwaves through the scientific community, and Kyree's name became synonymous with groundbreaking research. Despite the accolades, Kyree remained humble, always seeking to uncover more secrets of the ancient world.",
